WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.210
The ever-recognizable
Sakuragi Institute.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.340
What mysteries could
they be unsealing today?

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.590
Renji, what’s that?

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.220
It’s finally back from
being repaired...

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.930
This is Françoise’s favorite lamp!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.350
Come on, it’s lunchtime!

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.900
Does that taste good,
Françoise?

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.380
Coil! Magnet Pokémon!
Electric/Steel type!

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.630
It subsists on electricity!

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:13.510
As Coil flies, it emits electromagnetic waves
from the units on each side of its body!

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.010
Françoise sure is weird...

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.810
Yesterday it was eating a fan,
and before that... Was it a phone?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.400
Yeah. Who could imagine it only eats
from retro appliances...

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.820
Well, Françoise is a picky eater.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.780
It was a lot worse
when we first met.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.490
Oh? I’d like
to hear about that!

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.780
Then I’ll tell you the tale!

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:36.450
This was when Françoise and I–

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.490
Huh? A blackout?

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.000
It came back on.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.130
The blackout seems to have been
caused by a magnetic storm.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.130
A magnetic storm?

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.180
It’s a phenomenon caused by explosions
on the surface of the sun.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.890
They can damage the power grid,
or ruin delicate instruments.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.430
Huh...

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.890
Kikuna, everything okay?

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.560
That’s what I wanted to ask you!
Is Françoise okay?!

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.190
Huh?

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.570
Did something happen?

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.190
I’ll send you a video.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:11.280
There’s big trouble
in the city right now.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.780
What happened to you?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.080
What’s going on...?

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.930
What is this...?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.810
It’s receiving
a strange transmission...

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.020
That might be the reason
the Coil are behaving oddly.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:14.190
What is it, Pikachu?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.110
Françoise?!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.820
It’s not listening?

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.870
You should put it
in its Monster Ball for now.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.080
Françoise, return!

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.000
But why?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.330
Is the strange transmission
causing that, too?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.670
Drastic times call for...

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:40.800
Renji, what is that?!

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.800
Tinfoil!

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.810
That should block
the transmission!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.940
Tinfoil is amazing!

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.940
Still, it’s not like it
can block it out completely...

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.070
Hmm...

00:04:54.650 --> 00:05:00.450
It looks like strange Coil behavior
has only been reported in central Kuchiba City.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.990
You should be able to avoid the effects
if you head to the outskirts.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.620
Great idea, Director Sakuragi!

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.830
How about evacuating
for the time being?

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.380
It doesn’t want to?

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:15.750
Well, it’s been getting pickier
and pickier lately.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.720
Now it even wants all its things
to have a retro feel...

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.800
Its things too, huh...?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:23.680
I know!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.350
What?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.310
I covered up
the tinfoil with a hat.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.140
What is that thing?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.980
A doorknob cover.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.110
I guess kids these days
haven’t heard of them.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:38.860
Then let’s go!

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.360
Come on out, Kairyu!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.360
Flygon!

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.530
All right!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.870
Get on, Renji!

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:48.200
Huh? Ride that?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.410
We’ll get to
the outskirts in

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.120
Huh? Ride that?

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.300
I didn’t know you were
scared of heights, Renji...

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:02.050
I thought I’d be
able to tough it out,

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:05.140
but I’m so scared
I’m starting to feel faint...

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.600
If it’s getting to you,
you should think about something else.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.890
Something else?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.900
Tell me that tale from earlier!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:20.280
Oh, how Françoise and I met...

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:26.410
It all began the first
time I went into that café.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:28.950
Welcome!

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.460
This is a very calming place.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.380
Thank you.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:41.340
I love antiques, and can’t
resist collecting them.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.310
A Coil... Is it yours?

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:55.650
No. It’s just started coming
to this café lately.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:59.570
For whatever reason,
it seems to love that chandelier.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.440
Huh...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.610
Wild Coil usually eat
from power lines.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.450
You’re pretty unique.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.250
Guys!

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.080
It’s a Coil...

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.090
Think it’s gonna attack?

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.340
We better not provoke it.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.130
Hey, Go! Look to your side!

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.800
When did they get here?!

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.050
Hold on, this might not be
the best time for talking...

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.100
Let’s get out of here!

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:31.850
Right!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.690
Françoise!

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.200
Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.160
You okay?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.500
They ate the Electroweb!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.170
There’s more coming
from behind us!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:05.170
Ahh! They look really mad!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.800
They want Françoise!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:08.510
Huh? Why?

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.350
They might be trying
to force it to join them.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:15.430
Not a chance! I’m not letting
Françoise end up like that!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.060
Okay.
Kairyu, use Hurricane!

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:23.860
Satoshi!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.400
You go on ahead!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.740
I’ll hold them back!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.860
Got it!

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.200
Let’s go, Flygon!

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.160
Kairyu,
use Hurricane again!

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.740
Pikachu, use Iron Tail!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.620
We stand out
too much in the air.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.290
Thanks, Flygon.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.470
We can’t make any dumb moves...

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.300
Okay... Renji!

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.310
Hey!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.200
Follow me!

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.870
Thank you, Go.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.910
Let’s go, Françoise!

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.370
Pocket Monsters!

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.720
I can’t find any
other similar cases.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.310
How about you, Kikuna?

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:40.890
Right. I nearly have
this narrowed down...

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:42.850
Found it!

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:47.070
The strange transmission is coming
from above the city...

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.360
Wait, it’s coming from...

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.780
...space!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.950
Go, Aceburn!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.260
We’ll be too exposed
if we keep going.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.470
What do I do...?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.220
Hey, stop that!

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.820
It’s really made
this place its home.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.610
I could say the same thing
for you, Mr. Renji.

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.400
Well, it’s so comfortable here!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.910
Don’t you agree?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.410
Oh, now that’s unusual.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.790
Hey, welcome.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.250
What do you think of this?

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.130
Oh...

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.680
No interest, huh?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.560
It’s not too cramped in there,
is it, Françoise?

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.110
We’d stick out
if we started running.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.400
Let’s just walk past them.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.160
Oh, no!

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:22.620
Hurricane!

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.460
They just keep coming...!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:35.970
But we can’t let ‘em pass!

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.030
After them, Flygon!

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:01.780
This is hopeless...

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.750
Françoise...

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:08.750
Okay!
Supersonic Waves!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.060
Are they gone?

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:29.900
That café...

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.730
And so, please forgive me.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.360
But I have to
close down the café.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.490
Is that so...?

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:41.740
But I worry about
that little one.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.240
If only I had the means
to look after it myself.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.040
In that case,
may I take it in?

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:54.380
That’s... My, thank you.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.550
Oh, of course. If you’d like,
you may take that lamp too.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.430
Since the day
you offered it that lamp,

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:04.680
it’s taken a liking to it.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.480
Please use it
to make it a new home.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.410
You need to start
eating something...

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.660
What a mess...

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.450
I know you loved that chandelier,

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.790
but I never imagined you’d
refuse everything else...

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.250
It’s such a lovely lamp, though.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:34.920
Just give it a try...

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.180
Look, it’s snowing.

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.060
Hey, wait!

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:55.560
Oh, come on...

00:13:59.490 --> 00:14:01.700
Just a little bit further now...

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:07.950
Oh dear...

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.340
Françoise!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.340
Don’t worry about me!
Just run for it!

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.520
Françoise...

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.490
No...

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.950
Renji!

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.290
Sorry we’re late!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.710
Where’s Françoise?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.380
Up there?!

00:14:58.380 --> 00:15:00.550
Give Françoise back!

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.350
They’re sticking together!

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:11.680
Are their magnets going haywire?!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:12.600
No...

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.940
They’re evolving!

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.770
Huh? But...

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:22.150
Coil’s only evolutions are Rarecoil
and Jibacoil, yeah?!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.400
As far as we know.

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.780
But there’s so much we don’t know
about Pokémon’s capabilities.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.160
Absolutely anything could happen.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:32.540
Huh?

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.210
Then it could be some
never-seen-before Hyper-Rare–

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:37.540
No, Ultra-Rarecoil?!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:45.220
Director Sakuragi.

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.390
We found the source
of the transmission.

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:52.600
A man-made satellite malfunctioned
in the magnetic storm earlier,

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:56.060
and started transmitting
at the Kuchiba City area all on its own.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.270
A man-made satellite?!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.570
The Space Center is trying
to shut it down right now.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:04.360
We might not have time
to wait for that!

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.400
Huh?

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.860
The Coil forced Françoise
to join them!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:12.780
They’re turning into
a Hyper-Ultra-Rare-Rare-Rarecoil!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.290
What could that mean?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:22.340
Perhaps the transmission happened to be something
that induces Coil to evolve, by chance.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:25.090
But it overloaded them...

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:28.300
So they sought out even
more peers than usual,

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:32.350
and they’re trying to fuse
into an ultimate form.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.480
But if that happens,
Françoise will never come back.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.230
I’ll stop them!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.280
I need to get Françoise back,
somehow...

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.030
Renji...

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.960
Satoshi! Have Pikachu
use 100,000 Volts!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.170
Huh?

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:05.550
Evolution requires energy.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.800
When the Coil see Pikachu’s tasty-looking
electricity, they’ll jump at it.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:14.050
Except for one picky eater
who only likes retro appliances...

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:16.930
I get it!

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.560
Okay! Let’s do this, Pikachu!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:28.440
Right now, all I can do
is trust Françoise.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.780
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.710
We did it!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:01.100
They’re still not stopping?!

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:03.270
Renji!

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:10.070
Hey! Hey!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.120
It couldn’t be...

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.880
Hey!

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:31.670
Hey! Hey!

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.560
Where could you be?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:01.080
There you are.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.890
Look at the state I’m in
from searching for you.

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:22.890
You really must’ve loved
that chandelier.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.940
And if it was within my power,
I’d love to grant your wish.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:35.700
But for now, do you think you
can make do with this lamp?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.280
Focus on eating and
getting your strength back,

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:43.080
then we can look for
that chandelier together.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:20:00.970
Hey... Would you mind
if I called you Françoise?

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:16.150
F-Françoise...

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:21.490
You... are Françoise...

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.400
It’s back to normal.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.820
It’s a miracle.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.400
Welcome home.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.700
Was it a miracle?

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:05.080
Or was it the exact moment
the transmission shut down?

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:09.080
Either way, the rampage of the Coil
had come to an end.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:10.670
And...

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:13.960
Welcome back, manager!

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:18.550
Thanks to your support,
I was able to open this place again.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.930
More than anything,
I’m glad to see you’re doing well.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:25.060
Oh, Françoise!

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:26.470
Françoise?

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.600
Oh, I do apologize.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.440
I borrowed the name
of your café...

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:33.650
I see...

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:39.860
Well then, I hope the two of you enjoy your stay
here at Café Françoise.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:40.740
We will!

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.830
Go!

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.710
Kaiross is acting weird?

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:14.710
Yeah...

00:23:14.710 --> 00:23:17.710
She’s been really depressed
since a romantic rival showed up...

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:20.840
I want to cheer Kaiross on!

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:23.720
Hey! Have you heard
of Pokémon flower arranging?

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.470
You can beautifully decorate
Pokémon using flowers!

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:28.300
Decorating Pokémon
with flowers...

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:29.720
That’s it!

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:31.640
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:32.850
Heracross Loss,

00:23:32.850 --> 00:23:34.520
Lovey-Dovey Kaiross
